已按 CONTRIBUTING 指引发到 Discussions（issues 未启用）。
如果团队希望，我可以补一个带单测的正式 PR（但目前 CONTRIBUTING 说明不接受外部 PR，故先以讨论形式提交）。

反馈对象：deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness（dsh）
反馈日期：2026-08-15
提交人环境：Windows 10 (10.0.19044) / Node v24.14.1 / dsh 0.1.0-rc.6


一、问题概述（Summary）
在 Windows 上，将目录选择器固定为 browse 交互（网页内目录浏览框）后，点击进入用户主目录下的旧版 junction 目录（如 C:\Users\<用户名>\Application Data、C:\Users\<用户名>\Cookies 等）会直接报错：
cannot list C:\Users\beta\Application Data: EPERM: operation not permitted, opendir 'C:\Users\beta\Application Data'
cannot list C:\Users\beta\Cookies: EPERM: operation not permitted, opendir 'C:\Users\beta\Cookies'

这些目录是 Windows 为兼容旧程序保留的 junction（reparse point），分别指向 AppData\Roaming、AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\Windows\Cookies 等真实目录，普通用户完全可以访问（资源管理器、cmd 均可正常进入）。但 Node 的 fs.opendir/readdir 对 junction 路径本身直接返回 EPERM。

二、复现步骤（Steps to Reproduce）

Windows 系统，用户主目录存在旧版 junction（默认都有：Application Data、Cookies、Local Settings、My Documents、Recent 等）。
dsh web 组合使用 browse 目录选择器（@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-directory-picker-browse + @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-directory-picker-browse；即 dsh-host-directory-picker-auto 解析为 browse，或直接在配置中固定 browse）。
点击「新增工作区」→ 在网页目录浏览框中导航到主目录 → 点击 Application Data（或 Cookies、Local Settings 等任一 junction 行）。

实际行为：对话框顶部路径区显示 cannot list <junction路径>: EPERM: operation not permitted, opendir '<junction路径>'，无法进入该目录。
期望行为：与资源管理器一致，正常进入 junction 指向的真实目录（或至少不报 EPERM）。

三、根因分析（Root Cause）
3.1 Node 对 junction 路径的行为
在本机验证（Node v24.14.1）：



操作
对 C:\Users\beta\Application Data 的结果




fs.stat
OK（跟随 junction，isDirectory() === true）


fs.realpath
OK → C:\Users\beta\AppData\Roaming


fs.readdir
EPERM: operation not permitted, scandir


fs.opendir
EPERM: operation not permitted, opendir


fs.opendir(realpath(...))
OK



即：Node（libuv）对 Windows junction 路径的目录打开操作返回 EPERM，而路径解析（stat/realpath）正常。这属于 libuv/Node 在 Windows 上对 reparse point 的处理行为（junction 虽在 Dirent 中表现为 isSymbolicLink() === true，但按链接路径打开目录仍被拒绝）。
3.2 出错的代码位置
@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-directory-picker-browse 的 BrowseDirectoryPicker.list()（lib/index.js）：
const opening = opendir(target);
const level = await raceAbort(opening, signal).catch((error) => {
    opening.then((dir) => dir.close().catch(swallowCloseFailure), () => {});
    throw error;   // ← EPERM 直接冒泡
});
外层 catch 把它包装为：
throw new DirectoryPickerError("directory-unreadable", target, `cannot list ${target}: ${messageOf(error)}`);
于是客户端只看到 cannot list ... EPERM ...，没有任何可操作提示。
3.3 影响范围

任何 Windows 用户的主目录里点击 junction 行都会触发（Application Data、Cookies、Local Settings、My Documents、Recent、SendTo、Start Menu、Templates 等十几个旧版 junction 全部受影响）。
其他目录中的 junction（如 C:\Users\Public\Documents 等）同样受影响。
由于 browse 后端也服务于远程/无桌面场景，这个问题在 Windows 上具有普遍性。


四、建议修复（Suggested Fix）
方案（已本地验证）：EPERM 时经 realpath 解析后重试
在 list() 中，当 opendir 因 EPERM 失败且平台为 win32 时，先 realpath 解析 junction 到真实路径，再用真实路径重试一次；成功后列表行、面包屑、返回的 path 均使用解析后的真实路径（后续导航也不会再次踩到 junction）。
补丁（对 dsh-host-directory-picker-browse/lib/index.js）：
-import { mkdir, opendir, stat } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { mkdir, opendir, realpath, stat } from "node:fs/promises";
-		const target = resolve(path ?? home);
+		let target = resolve(path ?? home);
 		try {
 			const opening = opendir(target);
-			const level = await raceAbort(opening, signal).catch((error) => {
+			const level = await raceAbort(opening, signal).catch(async (error) => {
 				opening.then((dir) => dir.close().catch(swallowCloseFailure), () => {});
-				throw error;
+				// Windows legacy junctions (e.g. `C:\Users\<name>\Application
+				// Data` → `AppData\Roaming`) refuse directory opens through the
+				// junction path with EPERM; resolve to the real target and retry
+				// once so the level still lists (and rows/crumbs carry the real
+				// path, which also opens cleanly on later navigation).
+				if (process.platform !== "win32" || error?.code !== "EPERM") throw error;
+				let resolved;
+				try {
+					resolved = await realpath(target);
+				} catch {
+					throw error;
+				}
+				if (resolved === target) throw error;
+				target = resolved;
+				const retry = opendir(target);
+				return raceAbort(retry, signal).catch((retryError) => {
+					retry.then((dir) => dir.close().catch(swallowCloseFailure), () => {});
+					throw retryError;
+				});
 			});
备选方案（更彻底）

在 list() 入口对 win32 的 target 先做一次 realpath 规范化（所有路径都解析 junction），UI 行为一致且无重试路径；代价是多一次 syscall，且 resolve 不存在的路径时 realpath 会失败（需回退）。
或在上游目录选择 seam（dsh-host-directory-picker）约定：所有 Windows 路径统一走 realpath 后的规范形式。

修复验证
本地用修补后的包直接调用 list()，三组用例均通过：
OK   junction itself: path=C:\Users\beta\AppData\Roaming entries=135 crumbs=C:\ > Users > beta > AppData > Roaming
OK   home dir:        path=C:\Users\beta entries=73 crumbs=C:\ > Users > beta
OK   normal dir:      path=C:\Users\beta\AppData\Roaming entries=135 crumbs=C:\ > Users > beta > AppData > Roaming

注意：本地补丁改的是已安装包文件，dsh 升级会被覆盖，所以希望官方在下一版本中合入该修复。

Summary
@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-presets (AgentPresets.ensureStanding) does not dispose the replaced standing generation when a preset's composition file changes mid-process. The old generation's registered effects stay live, so a fresh mount of the same preset fails when its local plugin re-registers the same host route (webServer throws on duplicate) — the preset becomes unmountable until the process is restarted.
Environment

Package: @deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-presets 0.1.0-rc.6 (source dir packages/preset/agent-presets)
Profile: dsh web (Windows), DeepSeek Harness CLI 0.1.0-rc.6

Observed behavior

A locally authored preset (~/.dsh/.agent-presets/<id>/agent.cordis.yml) contains a preset-local plugin (name: './quota-dashboard-host.js') that registers webServer routes via ctx.effect(() => webServer.register({ kind: 'exact', path, handler })). A session starts on the preset → standing mount created, routes registered.
The preset's agent.cordis.yml is edited (any change — e.g. a persona text tweak).
Another session starts on the preset (or a host reader calls agentPresets.standingKeyFor(id)) → ensureStanding sees the composition stamp changed → it drops the standing-map entry and remounts a fresh generation.
The fresh generation's quota-dashboard-host plugin re-registers the same routes, but the old generation's routes are still live (its scope was never disposed) → mount fails:

agent-presets: preset "aicc-zhunao" failed to mount: failed to apply loader entry
quota-dashboard-host (./quota-dashboard-host-2.js):
webserver: duplicate exact route "/quota-center/data.json"
(C:\Users\ZHOU816\.dsh\.agent-presets\aicc-zhunao\agent.cordis.yml)


Only a process restart clears the stale routes and makes the preset mountable again.

Root cause
In ensureStanding (packages/preset/agent-presets):
async ensureStanding(preset) {
  const pending = this.standing.get(preset.id);
  if (pending !== void 0) {
    const mounted = await pending;
    const current = await compositionStamp(preset.path);
    if (current === void 0 || sameStamp(mounted.stamp, current)) return mounted;
    if (this.standing.get(preset.id) === pending) this.standing.delete(preset.id);
    return this.ensureStanding(preset);   // ← replaced generation is NOT disposed
  }
  ...
  } catch (error) {
    this.standing.delete(preset.id);
    await scope.dispose();                 // ← only the FAILURE path disposes
    throw error;
  }
The stale-generation path drops the map entry and remounts, but never calls scope.dispose() on the replaced mount, so every effect it registered (webServer routes, timers, listeners) stays registered for the process lifetime. The failure path correctly disposes — the success/remount path does not.
Note compositionStamp only stats the composition file (agent.cordis.yml), so edits to preset-local plugin files are never even detected; those rely on Node's module cache anyway (a same-path plugin file is not re-evaluated, which is why users "rename to bust the cache").
Suggested fix (preferred)
A standing generation should live exactly as long as (a) its composition is current, or (b) a live agent is still bound to it. Concretely:

Track the set of agent bindings per standing generation (the roster already keeps bindings).
When ensureStanding finds a stale generation, do not dispose it while any agent is bound (live sessions must keep working on the composition they started under, and their logged tool calls stay consistent with it).
Dispose the stale generation's scope once its last binding detaches; until then, ensureStanding returns the new generation for fresh agents.

Minimal alternative: on stamp mismatch, dispose the replaced scope immediately when no binding references it, and keep the current orphan behavior only for the (rare) case of bound agents — at least the common "edit preset, start new session" path then works without a restart.
Workaround used today
Collision-tolerant route registration in the preset-local plugin (skip register when webServer throws a duplicate … route for the same path) plus a plugin-file rename to break the module cache. This works but papers over the lifecycle leak and only helps plugins that can tolerate a skipped registration.
Related

Preset-local plugin file edits are not picked up in-process at all (stamp tracks only the composition file; module cache). Consider documenting that plugin-file changes require a restart, or extending the stamp/watch to the preset directory.

Failed to load plugins
@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation
@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-cordis
failed to apply loader entry f90db188 (@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation): single slot "details" already has a registration at priority 0 (registered by x6) — register at a different priority to shadow it (lowest renders)

Verified on master 47f9438. Duplicate search (preset switch / memory leak / agentPresets.select) found no prior coverage — #1524 and #1585 cover preset behavior (selection lost / live-switching), not this cleanup defect.
Summary
The documented per-session cleanup of the agentPresets.select serialization queue can never fire. packages/host/apiproxy/src/api-proxy.ts:3125-3132:
const queued = presetSwitches.get(sessionId) ?? Promise.resolve()
const turn = queued.then(swap)
presetSwitches.set(sessionId, turn.catch(() => undefined))
try {
  return await turn
} finally {
  if (presetSwitches.get(sessionId) === turn) presetSwitches.delete(sessionId)
}
The value stored in the Map is turn.catch(...) — a different promise object than turn. The finally identity check compares the stored catch-chained promise against the raw turn, so it is always false and the delete is unreachable dead code. Every session that ever selected a preset leaves one entry in presetSwitches: Map<SessionId, Promise> (plus its swallowed-rejection promise) for the lifetime of the host process — unbounded growth across distinct sessions.
Impact

Serialization itself stays correct (the chain resolves in order), so this is a low-severity resource leak, not a behavior bug.
The per-session cleanup contract is provably broken: long-lived host processes accumulate Map entries indefinitely.

Contrast with correct patterns in the same file
api-proxy.ts:1710-1718 and 2836-2843 chain promises the same way but never attempt identity-compare deletion — they are fine.
Suggested fix (either direction)

Store the raw turn and handle the rejection in the chain tail, or
Delete when the chain is idle (compare whether the stored tail has settled) instead of comparing object identity with a promise that was never stored.

Reproduction
Static proof — any single agentPresets.select call leaks one entry; nothing reclaims it before process exit. Visible with a heap snapshot diff after N distinct sessions select a preset.

Summary: workspace.rename() only updates display title, physical folder stays unchanged. When renaming a workspace in the DSH web UI, only workspace.json's 'title' field changes. The actual directory on disk keeps its old name and does not match the new display name.
Reproduction steps:

Create or open an existing workspace
Rename it to a different title via the web UI
Check the filesystem: the folder still has the OLD name, not the new one. Only workspace.json's 'title' field updated.

Root cause (dsh-workspace/lib/index.js line ~81):
async setTitle(title) {
await this.mutate((record) => ({...record, title})); // NO fs.rename! Just updates KV store.
}
The RPC handler in dsh-host-apiproxy only calls: await workspace.setTitle(title); with zero filesystem operations anywhere in the call chain.
Expected behavior: Physical folder name should update to match new display title.
Actual: Only DB record changed; folder stays as-is.
Suggested fix for setTitle():
async setTitle(newTitle) {
const oldPath = this.record.path;
const newPath = path.join(path.dirname(oldPath), newTitle);
if (oldPath !== newPath) {
await fs.rename(oldPath, newPath);    // rename physical folder
await this.mutate(record => ({...record, title: newTitle, path: newPath}));
} else {
await this.mutate(record => ({...record, title: newTitle}));
}
}
Important note for the fix: Changing physical directory without updating sessionHeaders' cwd would cause sessions to be filtered out by get sessionIds(). A safe implementation must either update affected session paths or reject renames when active sessions exist.
Environment: DSH v0.1.0-rc.6, @deepseek-ai/dsh-workspace + dsh-host-apiproxy (Linux x86_64).
This is a cosmetic-only bug - no data integrity issues but UI shows inconsistent names between workspace list and filesystem.

cordis_inspect_query 的 client 平台查询在无页面应答时永久挂起（无超时），整个 turn 冻结，只能靠 UI 停止或重启服务恢复。
复现、预期与验收
源码定位（供排查参考）：
@deepseek-ai/dsh-cordis-host-runner/lib/types/inspect-registry.js 的 queryClient()：pending Promise 只能被 resolveClientQuery()（页面应答且输出校验通过）或 abort 监听器 settle，不存在任何 timeout 路径。
resolveClientQuery() 对无效应答返回 accepted: false 且不清除 pending——页面应答了但输出校验失败时，同样会永久挂起。
@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-cordis/lib/index.js 中 cordis_inspect_query 的工具描述明确写着 “remains pending until a page answers or the Tool is cancelled”——与观察一致，但工具层同样没有超时兜底。

