@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-directory-picker-native/lib/worker.cjs, readUtf16():
function readUtf16(koffi, address) {
  const bytes = Buffer.from(koffi.view(address, 32768));
  let end = 0;
  while (end + 1 < bytes.length && bytes[end] !== 0) end += 2; // only checks the LOW byte
  return bytes.toString("utf16le", 0, end);
}
UTF-16LE stores 开 (U+5F00) as bytes 00 5F: the low byte is 0x00, so the
loop mistakes it for the NUL terminator and stops there. Any code point of the
form U+XX00 (开, 一, ...) triggers the same truncation. ASCII-only paths
are unaffected.
Minimal repro
const s = 'E:\\Projects\\00-软件开发';
const bytes = Buffer.from(s, 'utf16le');
let end = 0;
while (end + 1 < bytes.length && bytes[end] !== 0) end += 2;
console.log(bytes.toString('utf16le', 0, end)); // "E:\Projects\00-软件"
Suggested fix
Check both bytes of the code unit:
while (end + 1 < bytes.length && (bytes[end] !== 0 || bytes[end + 1] !== 0)) end += 2;

Environment: DSH 0.1.0-rc.5, web UI served over plain HTTP on a LAN IP hostname (e.g. http://<lan-ip>:3080).
Symptom: Opening the workspace directory picker (Add workspace) fails with crypto.randomUUID is not a function and cannot list directories. Any typed RPC through WebApiClient — host.listDirectory, host.pickDirectory, workspace.create — fails the same way.
Why: crypto.randomUUID is a secure-context-only Web API; browsers expose it only on HTTPS or loopback origins. Over plain HTTP on a non-loopback IP, window.isSecureContext === false and crypto.randomUUID is undefined. AbstractApiClient.mintRpcId() in packages/host/apiproxy/src/fetch/client.ts calls it directly, so every unary call mints its rpcId there and throws on such an origin.
The generic RPC path (packages/client/connection/src/client/rpc.ts) is already safe — it uses randomUuid() from random-uuid.ts, an RFC 4122 v4 UUID built on crypto.getRandomValues, which browsers do expose on insecure origins. Only the typed carrier misses it.
Proposed fix (one-liner): WebApiClient (the browser subclass, packages/client/connection/src/client/web-api-client.ts) should override:
protected override mintRpcId(): RpcId {
  return RpcId(randomUuid())
}
Also worth hardening while touching this: browserDraftAttachment in packages/client/ui-conversation/src/client/service.ts uses crypto.randomUUID() for draft attachment ids — same failure on such an origin.
I verified the fix locally: the picker browses and selects a workspace over plain-HTTP-on-IP with zero console errors, with the existing test suite passing. Happy to adapt to whatever the team prefers once external PRs open up.

问题
Profile 的 cordis.patch.yml 里给 agent-presets 配置了自定义 roots（例如工作区共享的 preset 目录）后，静态配置组合（dsh --dump-config）显示正确，但实际启动后 Web 界面的 Agent 预设选择器里，所有自定义 preset 都不见了，只剩 4 个 shipped 预设。
根因
apps/cli/src/profile-boot.ts 的 composeProfile() 在给 agent-presets 注入 app 自有的 shipped preset 目录时，用了整体替换而不是追加：
if (rows.has('agent-presets')) {
  composedOverlays.push({
    id: 'agent-presets',
    config: {
      ...(rows.get('agent-presets')?.config ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>,
      roots: [{ path: SHIPPED_PRESET_ROOT, trust: 'system' }],
    },
  })
}
这一行 roots: [{ path: SHIPPED_PRESET_ROOT, trust: 'system' }] 把用户 patch 层已经组合好的 roots 数组整个覆盖掉，只剩 shipped root 这一条。而 dsh --dump-config（apps/cli/src/dump-config.ts）走的是另一条不含这段 overlay 的路径，所以静态 dump 显示正常，实际 boot（runProfile → composeProfile）却把用户配置的 roots 吞掉了。
复现

~/.dsh/profiles/<profile>/cordis.patch.yml 里给 agent-presets 配置：
- id: agent-presets
  config:
    default: standard
    roots:
      - path: /path/to/shared/presets
        trust: user
    includeUserRoot: true

dsh --profile <profile> --dump-config 能看到这条 roots 配置正确保留。
启动 dsh <profile>，Web 界面 Agent 预设下拉里，/path/to/shared/presets 下的自定义 preset 全部不可见（ctx.agentPresets.roots 运行时读到的只有 shipped root + .agent-presets user root）。

已验证的修复
把整体替换改成追加（shipped root 在前，保留部署优先级；配置 roots 追加在后）：
export function prependShippedAgentPresetRoot(config: Record<string, unknown>): PatchOptions {
  const configuredRoots = config.roots
  if (configuredRoots !== undefined && !Array.isArray(configuredRoots)) {
    throw new TypeError('dsh: agent-presets config.roots must be an array')
  }
  return {
    id: 'agent-presets',
    config: {
      ...config,
      roots: [
        { path: SHIPPED_PRESET_ROOT, trust: 'system' },
        ...(configuredRoots ?? []),
      ],
    },
  }
}
本地验证：修复前 Web 界面预设下拉只有 4 个 shipped 预设；应用修复并重启后，14 个自定义 workspace 预设全部正常出现，且 shipped 预设仍保持 id 冲突时的优先级。
分支（含测试）：fix/preserve-profile-agent-preset-roots，在我的 fork：https://github.com/ankye/deepseek-harness/tree/fix/preserve-profile-agent-preset-roots
了解到目前不接受外部 PR，先在这里报告，供团队参考评估是否采纳类似修复。

Component: dsh-client-ui-deliverables (Web UI)
Version: 0.1.0-rc.8
Platform: macOS (confirmed; likely affects all platforms)
What happens
When clicking the "在文件夹中显示" / "Show in Folder" button on a produced-files row, the button hardcodes openFile('.'), which resolves to the session's workspace root (e.g., /Users/xxx/AiComing) rather than the directory containing the produced files (e.g., /Users/xxx/AiComing/output/).
Root Cause
In packages/client/ui-deliverables/src/client/ProducedFiles.tsx:
{hidden > 0 && canOpenPath && (
  <button type="button" className={css.showFolder} onClick={() => { openFile('.') }}>
    {t('produced.showInFolder')}
  </button>
)}
The '.' path goes through resolveWorkspacePath(cwd, '.') which naively concatenates cwd + '/.', then hits the Host's openPath RPC. This opens the workspace root — not the folder containing the turn's produced files.
Expected Behavior
The button should open the common parent directory of the produced files, or the first produced file's parent directory.
Proposed Fix
Add a parentPath() helper in turn-deliverables.ts:
/** Return the parent directory of a path, handling both separators and trailing slashes. */
export function parentPath(path: string): string {
  const trimmed = path.replace(/[/\\]+$/, '')
  const lastSlash = Math.max(trimmed.lastIndexOf('/'), trimmed.lastIndexOf('\\'))
  return lastSlash <= 0 ? '.' : trimmed.slice(0, lastSlash)
}
Then in ProducedFiles.tsx:
import { basename, parentPath } from './turn-deliverables.ts'

// In the component:
{hidden > 0 && canOpenPath && (
  <button
    type="button"
    className={css.showFolder}
    onClick={() => { openFile(parentPath(paths[0])) }}
  >
    {t('produced.showInFolder')}
  </button>
)}
Additional Note
The existing test in produced-files.client.spec.tsx asserts openFile was called with '.', which locks in the buggy behavior:
fireEvent.click(showFolder)
expect(openFile).toHaveBeenLastCalledWith('.')
This assertion should be updated to verify the correct parent path resolution.

Bug
When navigating or interacting with the DSH web UI, the agent turn crashes with:
Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'kind')

The UI shows "This turn failed" and requires clicking "continue" to recover.
Root Cause
In packages/extensions/cordis-client-runner/src/client/providers.ts, the compactSlotTree() function (line ~188) assumes the node parameter is always defined:
function compactSlotTree(node: LiveSlotNode): JsonValue {
  // ...
  return {
    name: node.name,
    kind: node.kind,  // ← crashes here if node is undefined
    // ...
  }
}
This can happen during race conditions when slots are being registered/unregistered.
Suggested Fix
Add defensive null checks:
function compactSlotTree(node: LiveSlotNode | undefined): JsonValue | undefined {
  if (node === undefined) return undefined
  // ... rest unchanged ...
  children: node.children.map(compactSlotTree).filter((child): child is JsonValue => child !== undefined),
}
And update the caller at line ~120:
trees: trees.map(compactSlotTree).filter((tree): tree is JsonValue => tree !== undefined),
Reproduction
The crash occurred after running a bash command (git push) in the web UI. The command completed successfully but the turn crashed during result rendering.
Environment

DSH version: 0.1.1-rc.2
Browser: Chrome
Platform: Linux (Docker container)

