Sessions whose stored cwd matches a Workspace are not grouped under it ("Ungrouped"), because adoption only runs during the one-time bootstrap
Where: packages/workspace/workspace/src/index.ts (WorkspaceRegistry[Service.init], bootstrap) + packages/workspace/workspace/src/entity.ts (WorkspaceEntity.attachSession, mutate)
Environment: desktop runtime @deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop-runtime 0.2.0-rc.2 (also present in the published CLI @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.1); Windows; verified against master (packages/workspace/workspace/src/index.ts, blob 4b4176c5).
Summary
A session is only ever attached to a workspace when SessionController.create() is called with an explicit workspaceId (or when a fork child attaches). There is no recovery path afterwards, so a session that starts any other way — or whose workspace accounting is pruned once — stays in Ungrouped forever, even though its stored header cwd is exactly the workspace path.
Reproduction / observed data
On a machine with one Workspace E:\...\Project\EOS registered since first use (state.initialized === true):




count




sessions listed in storages/workspace.json for that workspace
22


sessions whose per-session cache identity.cwd is that same path, but which appear in no workspace
31



The ungrouped sessions' stored headers are correct, e.g.
{"type":"session","version":4,"id":"session-09f3f60d-...","cwd":"D:\\Larry\\Documents\\Project\\EOS","isSeeded":false}
so indexHeader resolves them to the workspace path and get sessionIds() would include them — but they were never added to record.sessionIds in the first place.
Root cause

Adoption by canonical cwd lives in bootstrap(), which [Service.init] calls only while the registry is uninitialized:

if (!this.state.initialized) {
  const headers = await this.listStoredHeaders()
  await this.replaceHeaderIndex(headers)
  await this.bootstrap(headers)
} else if (this.table.size > 0) {
  await this.replaceHeaderIndex(await this.listStoredHeaders())
}
Once initialized: true is durable (normal after first use), sessionPaths is rebuilt but never reconciled with workspace membership. A session created without a workspaceId is therefore permanently loose.

Membership is pruned against that rebuilt index on every write, so a loose id that is not in the index is silently dropped:

// entity.ts — mutate()
const sessionIds = changed.sessionIds.filter(
  id => this.host.sessionPath(id) === changed.path,
)

attachSession then refuses to put it back, because its guard reads the raw snapshot rather than the filtered projection:

async attachSession(sessionId: SessionId): Promise<void> {
  // Validation is skipped when the settled snapshot already accounts the
  // id: the cwd fact was checked when it first attached and both inputs
  // (stored header cwd, workspace path) are immutable. Membership itself is
  // decided on the write chain inside `mutate`, never on this snapshot.
  if (!this.record.sessionIds.includes(sessionId)) { ... }
  await this.mutate(record => record.sessionIds.includes(sessionId)
    ? record
    : { ...record, sessionIds: [sessionId, ...record.sessionIds] })
}
this.record.sessionIds is the unfiltered stored array; get sessionIds() filters it by host.sessionPath(id) === record.path. A pruned/never-added id is absent from the filtered view but may be present in the raw one — so the early return skips re-validation and mutate finds the id already present and writes nothing. The result is a session that is visible in the sidebar (the list surface) but accounted to no group.
Note also that the justification "both inputs … are immutable" does not hold for the index: host.sessionPath(id) returns undefined whenever the header was absent from that process's index (header not in the persisted listing yet, cwd unresolvable, directory temporarily missing). The startup order makes this reachable: replaceHeaderIndex(...) runs before indexLiveSessions(), so any write that lands in between prunes candidates whose path is not yet indexed.
Suggested fix
Reconcile membership on every registry open, not only the first. Reusing the existing bootstrap loop is enough and needs no new data:
await this.indexLiveSessions()
// Adopt stored sessions whose canonical cwd matches a registered workspace but
// that no workspace accounts for (e.g. created without a workspaceId). Without
// this, membership is only ever established at create time and a pruned or
// never-attached session stays ungrouped forever.
await this.adoptLooseSessions()
this.rebuildEntities()
this.validateStoredState(this.requireState())
this.reportFilteredCandidates()
with adoptLooseSessions() = the historical half of bootstrap() restricted to already-registered paths (skip sessions already accounted for by any workspace; skip path mismatch or unresolvable cwd with a logger.warn).
Two related hardening points worth considering in the same change:

make attachSession's guard consult the same projection as get sessionIds() (re-validate when the id is not currently a member), so an explicit re-attach always works;
or reject an attach whose cwd does not match instead of writing an entry that mutate will immediately prune (today the write can silently no-op).

Workaround (for anyone hitting this before a fix)
storages/workspace.json is the durable registry. Moving a session id into the target workspace's sessionIds — via the UI, or by adding it to the array while the app is stopped — restores grouping, since the read projection only filters by path.
Verification of the workaround fix
Patching only WorkspaceRegistry[Service.init] in a packaged build to run the adoption step on every open (node --check clean, archive byte length unchanged, deterministic replay from a backup) grouped all 31 previously ungrouped sessions under the workspace on restart.

中文摘要：会话只有在「带 workspaceId 创建」时才会被挂进工作区；按 cwd 自动收编的逻辑（bootstrap）只在注册表首次初始化时执行一次，之后 initialized: true 便不再收编。同时 attachSession 的守卫读的是未过滤的原始快照，而读取侧的 sessionIds 是按规范路径过滤的 —— 于是被剪掉/从未加入的会话再也挂不回去，表现为「工作目录明明匹配，却一直待在未分组」。实测：一个工作区只收编了 22 个会话，另有 31 个 cwd 完全一致的会话遗留在未分组。建议把收编改成每次打开注册表都执行。

[Bug] subagent outcome drops turn-end error detail, so 429/quota failures arrive opaque
Component: @deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-in-process-driver
Status: present in published dsh-subagent-in-process-driver@0.2.0-rc.2
What happens
A settled child is returned as { output, stopReason }, where stopReason is produced by flattening the turn-end reason to a bare kind:
const recorded = toStopReason(lastEnd?.data.reason);
...
return { output, stopReason };
The turn-end reason carries the actual failure detail — message, detail, status, statusCode, code — which is where provider 429 / quota-exhaustion surfaces. All of it is discarded, so the parent agent cannot distinguish rate limiting from a crash or a normal error, and cannot decide whether to retry, switch models, or give up.
Expected
The settled outcome should retain enough detail to diagnose the failure, or at minimum expose a bounded diagnostic string.
Suggested change
Build a bounded diagnostic from the reason and attach it to the returned value:
function stopReasonErrorDetail(reason) {
  if (reason?.kind === "completed" || reason == null) return undefined;
  const parts = [String(reason.kind ?? "error")];
  for (const key of ["message", "detail", "status", "statusCode", "code"]) {
    const value = reason[key];
    if (value !== undefined && value !== null && String(value).length > 0) parts.push(key + ": " + String(value).slice(0, 500));
  }
  return parts.join(" | ");
}
We currently carry this as a local patch; it can be dropped once handled upstream.

Auto review silently turns into Full access after restarting the DSH desktop client
Environment

App: @deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop 0.2.0-rc.2 (Windows x64, Electron 44, Node 24)
Profile: desktop
Bundles include @deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-auto-review
Reproduced with a normal desktop restart (close the client, start it again)

Steps to reproduce

Open a session in the desktop client.
Select the experimental Auto review preset in the permission picker and confirm the risk prompt.
Let at least one tool call run under Auto review.
Close the desktop client completely.
Start the desktop client again and open the same session.

Actual behavior
The session is now in Full access, with no user prompt and no visible notice event. The previously selected Auto review is gone.
Expected behavior
The persisted Auto selection should either be restored when the Auto review layer is still mounted, or the user should be asked before a silently persisted Full-access migration.
Root cause
@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-auto-review registers a disposal effect in packages/experimental/auto-review/src/index.ts:
yield async () => {
  accepting = false
  try {
    for (const session of ctx.sessions.list()) {
      if (permissionPresets.current(session) !== AUTO_PRESET) continue
      permissionPresets.set(session, 'danger-full-access')
    }
  } finally {
    lifecycle.abort(new Error('auto-review integration disposed'))
    await Promise.allSettled([...active])
  }
}
That migration is meant for a live plugin unload (remove/disable Auto review while the host keeps running). But the same disposal runs during the whole host shutdown:

The desktop host calls application.shutdown.shutdown(0) from @deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop-host.
Cordis unloads the root fiber; the root fiber state becomes UNLOADING before child disposers run.
The Auto review plugin disposer still sees its live sessions in ctx.sessions.list().
It calls permissionPresets.set(session, 'danger-full-access'), which appends durable permission/preset, sandbox/mode, and approval/policy events to the session log.
On the next launch the session restores those persisted knob values, so the user sees Full access with no prompt.

So a client restart performs a persistent permission downgrade that the user never requested.
Suggested upstream fix
Only run the full-access migration when the root fiber is still ACTIVE, i.e. when the Auto review integration is being unloaded at runtime while the host itself keeps running.
--- a/packages/experimental/auto-review/src/index.ts
+++ b/packages/experimental/auto-review/src/index.ts
@@ -727,10 +727,15 @@ export function apply(ctx: Context): void {
     yield async () => {
       accepting = false
       try {
-        for (const session of ctx.sessions.list()) {
-          if (permissionPresets.current(session) !== AUTO_PRESET) continue
-          permissionPresets.set(session, 'danger-full-access')
+        // During a whole-host shutdown the root fiber is no longer ACTIVE.
+        // Migrating then would persist Full access over a stored Auto
+        // selection without any user action; only a live integration
+        // unload needs the migration.
+        if (ctx.root.fiber.state === FiberState.ACTIVE) {
+          for (const session of ctx.sessions.list()) {
+            if (permissionPresets.current(session) !== AUTO_PRESET) continue
+            permissionPresets.set(session, 'danger-full-access')
+          }
         }
       } finally {
         lifecycle.abort(new Error('auto-review integration disposed'))
FiberState.ACTIVE is 2; importing the enum from @deepseek-ai/cordis is preferable if it is exported. A numeric comparison (ctx.root.fiber.state === 2) is equivalent and avoids a new import.
Local workaround
A small host-profile plugin, dsh-auto-review-restart-fix, wraps ctx.permissionPresets.set and drops preset writes whenever ctx.root.fiber.state !== ACTIVE. Mount it before @deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-auto-review in dsh.profile.bundles so its fiber disposes after the Auto review fiber during shutdown.
Evidence

@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-auto-review/lib/index.js (compiled 0.2.0-rc.2) lines around the auto-review lifecycle effect.
@deepseek-ai/dsh-permission-presets/lib/index.js PermissionPresetService.set() → apply() → session.append('permission/preset', ...).
@deepseek-ai/cordis/src/fiber.ts: FiberState and _unload() run disposers while the owning fiber is UNLOADING; the root stays ACTIVE only for runtime plugin unloads.
@deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop-host/lib/index.js stop() → application.shutdown.shutdown(0).

Impact

Data loss: a stored Auto selection is overwritten by a silent Full-access migration on every app quit.
Security: the next session runs with more privilege than the user selected, and the change is not surfaced.
It affects any desktop/web profile that mounts the experimental Auto review bundle.

Composer, session A: type some text and attach an image (don't send). Switch to another session, then back — the text is still there, the image is gone. Windows, 0.2.0-rc.2.
The text survives because it lives in the per-session persisted store (packages/client/ui-conversation/src/client/stores.ts: init: () => ({ draft: '', view: null, viewRequest: null })). Attachment ids live on the InputShell instance (input/facade.ts: private attachmentIds: readonly DraftAttachmentId[] = []), and the shell rides the session scope fiber, whose teardown releases them (input/hub.ts: const drafts = shell.dispose(), then releaseDraftAttachment per id). That release is not just a dropped reference: it deletes from draftAttachments and revokes the preview URL.
What makes me unsure whether this is intended: switching workspace carries attachments across explicitly —
// input/apply.ts — selectWorkspace
const draft = from.snapshot.draft
const attachmentIds = from.snapshot.attachmentIds
const next = inputHub.shell(nextId)
if (attachmentIds.length === 0 || next.addAttachments(attachmentIds)) {
  concreteConversation(ctx).rebindDraftFiles(nextId, attachmentIds)
  // …then removes them from the source shell…
}
— while switching session has no equivalent step. From the user's side both actions are "go read another conversation".
So: is surviving a session switch deliberately out of scope for draft attachments, or does the session path just lack the carry-over the workspace path has? Either answer settles it for me — if it's out of scope I will document the behavior on our side rather than treat it as a defect.
(Behavior reported by a user of our desktop shell on 0.2.0-rc.2; the code paths above come from reading that version's client sources.)

报告对象：DeepSeek Harness 官方（github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness）
DSH 版本：0.2.0-rc.2
组件：@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-deepseek（约 lib/index.js L1666–L1693）
日期：2026-10-07
严重级别：中高（会话永久不可用，用户无法自救，且错误信息无助于定位）

一、摘要
当请求体中任一消息文本含孤立代理项（lone surrogate，如 \uDD16）时，DeepSeek messages 接口返回 400 INVALID_REQUEST。适配器在 buildMessages 阶段已有多重结构校验（tool_call 配对、role 合并等），但没有对文本做 Unicode 合法性校验或清洗，因此：

非法字符原样上线，被服务端拒绝；
报错被统一包装为 DeepSeek Messages request failed (400)，用户与开发者都无法得知真正原因；
更严重的是，坏字符已经写入会话历史，此后每轮请求都会重发它，导致该会话永久失败、重试无效；若污染源来自每轮注入的内容（如动态快照），新开会话同样复发——用户完全无法自救。

二、真实事故（本机完整复现）
背景：第三方记忆插件 @a9i5k4/dsh-auto-memory 用 UTF-16 code unit 计数做截断，把日志里的 🤖（0xD83E 0xDD16）从代理对中间切开，留下 0xDD16，写入了每轮注入的 user-role 动态快照。
现象：

会话 session-2c69b355：turn 1–29 全部 completed，turn 30 起每一轮在 step 起点即 400
重试同一轮必然失败；用户连续追问（"为什么运行失败了"、"？"）全部失败
新开会话 session-fe406bc0（turn 1 step 6）、session-d1b8e194 同样复发

证据：解压会话记录后扫描全部 1,255 个事件：
seq=1216 LONE_SURROGATES=1 -> [{"i":910,"code":"dd16","low":true}]
total events containing lone surrogates: 1

含孤立代理的事件恰好只有 1 个，正是唯一失败的那次请求。
对应的失败事件：
{"type":"assistant/attempt","seq":1251,"time":...,
 "data":{"turn":34,"step":1,"stream":[{"type":"chunk","chunk":{"type":"finish",
 "reason":{"kind":"error","failure":{
   "message":"DeepSeek Messages request failed (400)",
   "code":"INVALID_REQUEST","status":400}}}}]}}
三、问题一：适配器缺少 Unicode 合法性校验
@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-deepseek/lib/index.js 中，buildMessages 在 L1682–L1693 已做结构校验：
let pending = new Set();
for (const message of messages) if (message.role === "assistant") {
  const calls = message.content.filter((block) => block.type === "tool_use");
  pending = new Set(calls.map((block) => block.id));
  if (pending.size !== calls.length) throw new LlmError("DeepSeek Messages duplicate tool call id", "INVALID_REQUEST");
} else if (message.role === "user") {
  const results = message.content.filter((block) => block.type === "tool_result");
  for (const result of results) if (!pending.delete(result.tool_use_id)) throw new LlmError("DeepSeek Messages tool result has no matching call", "INVALID_REQUEST");
  if (pending.size > 0) throw new LlmError("DeepSeek Messages tool calls need immediate results", "INVALID_REQUEST");
  message.content = [...results, ...message.content.filter((block) => block.type !== "tool_result")];
}
if (pending.size > 0) throw new LlmError("DeepSeek Messages history ends with unresolved tools", "INVALID_REQUEST");
但没有等价的文本层校验。 建议在发送前增加：
// 检出孤立代理并给出可定位的错误
const findLoneSurrogate = (s) => {
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const c = s.charCodeAt(i);
    if (c >= 0xd800 && c <= 0xdbff) {
      const n = s.charCodeAt(i + 1);
      if (!(n >= 0xdc00 && n <= 0xdfff)) return i; else i++;
    } else if (c >= 0xdc00 && c <= 0xdfff) return i;
  }
  return -1;
};
并在发现时抛出带定位信息的错误，例如：
DeepSeek Messages message[12] contains a lone surrogate at offset 910 (0xdd16)

这样开发者一眼可知是「哪个消息、哪个偏移、什么字符」，而不是面对笼统的 400。

关于「响应体是否含更详细信息」：DeepSeek 服务端对 400 可能返回了具体原因（如 invalid unicode），但 DSH 当前把它统一包装成 request failed (400)，具体 body 未能透出到会话记录或用户可见界面。建议：

在会话日志中保留服务端返回的原始 error.message/body；
在 UI 上展示可读原因。这会让本类问题的排查从数小时缩短到数秒。


四、问题二（更关键）：坏内容进历史后不可恢复，且无自愈机制
本次事故最严重的部分不是「一次请求失败」，而是：

坏字符被写入会话历史（user/message 事件，带 surfaceOp: "append"），此后每轮请求都会重发整段历史；
因此失败永久化：turn 30 之后每一轮都在 step 起点即 400，重试无效；
若污染来源是每轮注入的内容（本例是动态快照 runtime-context），新开会话会在下一处同样位置复发。

用户侧完全无解：既不能重试，也不能靠开新会话绕过，且界面上没有任何提示指向真正原因。用户只能放弃整个会话。
建议：

发送前清洗（推荐）：对出站消息做一次 Unicode 规范化，将孤立代理替换为 U+FFFD，并在日志中记录「已清洗 N 处非法字符」。这能让会话自愈而非永久损坏。
或拒绝并给出可操作提示：明确告知「第 X 条消息含非法字符，建议开启新会话或使用 /compact 清理历史」，而不是笼统的 400。
压缩/裁剪路径也应接入同一清洗：dsh-compaction-basic、dsh-compaction-tool-result-pruner 在处理历史时若同样按 code unit 切分，也会引入同类坏字符。建议在其出口统一清洗。

五、问题三：注入时机的健壮性（相关但独立）
排查中还观察到：动态快照（runtime-context）由 dsh-agent-loop 的 preStep()（L902–925）在每个 step 开头生成，并以 user/message 追加（L917 [...claimed, context]、L1061 落盘）。当上一步刚以 tool/result 结束时，序列为：
assistant(tool_calls) → tool(result) → user(runtime-context snapshot)

在适配器 L1673–1675，tool 消息在 wire 上映射为 user 角色，且相邻同 role 消息会被合并：
const wireRole = message.role === "tool" ? "user" : message.role;
const previous = messages.at(-1);
if (previous?.role === wireRole) previous.content.push(...content);
二者合并后，L1688–1691 的 tool_result 配对校验在边界情形下会更脆弱。

说明：本次事故的直接原因是非法 Unicode（已用全切点穷举证明：27,234 个切点中仅 1 处产生坏字符，且与失败请求中的 0xdd16 逐位一致）。上述时机问题不是本次直接致因（实测同一模式下有 24 次「快照紧跟 tool/result」均正常），但它降低了系统的容错度——一旦文本层出问题，这个位置更容易放大为整轮失败。建议一并考虑：快照不宜插入 tool 结果与下一个 assistant 之间。

六、复现步骤（最小）

任意途径让会话历史中出现一条含孤立代理的消息。可用插件注入（本例），或在自定义工具输出中返回：

"\uDD16"     // 孤立低代理

该内容进入 user/message 并落盘；
下一轮请求即返回 400 INVALID_REQUEST；
此后每一轮都失败，重试无效；
若该内容来自每轮注入，新开会话仍会复发。

验证脚本（检出会话中的孤立代理）：
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
const text = readFileSync(transcriptPath, "utf8");
let n = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
  const c = text.charCodeAt(i);
  if (c >= 0xd800 && c <= 0xdbff) {
    const x = text.charCodeAt(i + 1);
    if (!(x >= 0xdc00 && x <= 0xdfff)) n++; else i++;
  } else if (c >= 0xdc00 && c <= 0xdfff) n++;
}
console.log("lone surrogates:", n);
七、附带发现的排查障碍（建议改进）
排查本次问题耗时较长，主要卡点如下，建议一并优化：


会话记录格式不便读取：~/.dsh/sessions/<ws>/<sid>/session.v4.jsonl.zstd 是多帧串联 zstd（一个事件一帧），zlib.zstdDecompressSync(整文件) 只能解出第一帧（约 200 字节的会话头）。需扫描 magic 28 B5 2F FD 逐帧解压才能拿到全文（实测大会话 708 帧 / 5.2 MB）。
→ 建议：提供官方导出/查看命令（如 dsh session export --jsonl），或提供带帧遍历的解压工具。


错误信息缺上下文：request failed (400) 未附带服务端 body、消息索引或字符偏移。
→ 建议：错误中包含服务端原始信息 + 定位。


无「历史体检」入口：污染后用户无法自查。
→ 建议：提供 dsh session doctor <id> 之类命令，扫描孤立代理/未配对 tool_call 等结构问题并给出修复建议。



附：本次事故的处理与验证（供参考）
用户侧已通过修补插件解决（详见 BUG报告_记忆插件_emoji截断_20261007.md），补丁后验证：

真实日志 27,234 个切点全穷举：裸 slice 1 处产生孤立代理，安全截断 0 处
合法文本零损伤（逐字节相同）、emoji 原样保留、幂等
node --check 通过

但对 DSH 而言，根因在于「出站文本未做 Unicode 校验/清洗」——即使第三方插件修好，任何自定义工具输出、MCP 返回、文件读取都可能引入同类字符。建议在适配器层做统一防御。

同时报错, 挂掉
AI分析的结果：
经过代码排查，你的判断完全正确。
确实存在这个问题：选择 gemini 4 argon（如 gemini-4-argon）时，系统会将其错误判定为使用 thinkingBudget（基于 token 数量的预算），而不是 thinkingLevel（离散等级），从而向 Google API 发送了带有 thinkingBudget 的配置，导致 Google API 报错拒绝。

一、根本原因定位
核心问题出在底层依赖库 @earendil-works/pi-ai（位于 node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-ai/dist/api/google-shared.js）的 usesGoogleThinkingLevel 判定函数中。
1. 判定函数写死了 gemini-3 和 pro|flash
在 google-shared.js 第 37–47 行：
export function usesGoogleThinkingLevel(model) {
    const id = model.id.toLowerCase();
    return (
        // Match Gemini 3 Pro/Flash IDs with or without a minor version, such as
        // gemini-3-flash-preview, gemini-3.1-pro-preview, and gemini-3.8-flash.
        /gemini-3(?:\.\d+)?-(?:pro|flash)/.test(id) ||
        id === "gemini-flash-latest" ||
        id === "gemini-flash-lite-latest" ||
        // Match both hosted Gemma 4 naming forms: gemma-4-* and gemma4-*.
        /gemma-?4/.test(id)
    );
}

该正则 /gemini-3(?:\.\d+)?-(?:pro|flash)/：

主版本号写死了 3，无法匹配 gemini-4；
模型型号写死了 pro|flash，无法匹配 argon。


因此，当传入 gemini-4-argon 时，usesGoogleThinkingLevel(model) 返回了 false。

2. 对比：同文件其他函数已经支持了 Gemini 4+
在同一个文件 google-shared.js 中，其他能力判定（如 requiresToolCallId、supportsGoogleStrictToolSampling）都使用了通用的版本解析逻辑：
function getGeminiMajorVersion(modelId) {
    const match = modelId.toLowerCase().match(/^gemini(?:-live)?-(\d+)/);
    if (!match) return undefined;
    return Number.parseInt(match[1], 10);
}
// 只要 >= 3，即 Gemini 3、Gemini 4 及后续版本都视为支持
return geminiMajorVersion !== undefined && geminiMajorVersion >= 3;
唯独 usesGoogleThinkingLevel 使用了过于狭窄的硬编码正则。

二、调用链与报错过程
在 google-vertex.js 和 google-generative-ai.js 中：


分支流向了 thinkingBudget：
if (usesGoogleThinkingLevel(model)) {
    return stream(model, context, {
        ...base,
        thinking: {
            enabled: true,
            level: toGoogleThinkingLevel(resolvedLevel),
        },
    });
}

// ❌ 因为返回 false，走到了此分支：
return stream(model, context, {
    ...base,
    thinking: {
        enabled: true,
        budgetTokens: getGoogleBudget(model, resolvedLevel, options.thinkingBudgets),
    },
});


组装请求体生成了 thinkingBudget：
在 stream 的 buildParams 中：
if (options.thinking?.enabled && model.reasoning) {
    const thinkingConfig = { includeThoughts: true };
    if (options.thinking.level !== undefined) {
        thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel = toGoogleSdkThinkingLevel(options.thinking.level);
    } else if (options.thinking.budgetTokens !== undefined) {
        // ❌ 被赋值为 thinkingBudget
        thinkingConfig.thinkingBudget = options.thinking.budgetTokens;
    }
    config.thinkingConfig = thinkingConfig;
}


Google API 报错：
Gemini 4 系列（Argon）与 Gemini 3 一样，在 API 协议上只支持离散的 thinkingLevel（MINIMAL / LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH），不支持 Gemini 2.5 时代的 thinkingBudget（token 整数）。向 Google 传入 thinkingBudget 会直接触发 400 参数校验错误（如 thinking_budget is not supported for gemini-4-argon 或 unsupported field: thinkingBudget）。



三、修复建议
可以通过项目的 pnpm patch 机制（在 patches/@earendil-works__pi-ai@1.1.0.patch 中）对 @earendil-works/pi-ai 的 dist/api/google-shared.js 打补丁，将 usesGoogleThinkingLevel 的判定放宽：
export function usesGoogleThinkingLevel(model) {
    const id = model.id.toLowerCase();
    const geminiMajorVersion = getGeminiMajorVersion(id);
    return (
        // 1. 只要是 Gemini 3 或更高版本（包含 Gemini 4 / Argon）
        (geminiMajorVersion !== undefined && geminiMajorVersion >= 3) ||
        // 2. 匹配 argon 别名或未带版本号的命名
        id.includes("argon") ||
        id === "gemini-flash-latest" ||
        id === "gemini-flash-lite-latest" ||
        /gemma-?4/.test(id) ||
        // 3. 或者模型元数据中显式声明了 thinkingLevelMap
        model.thinkingLevelMap !== undefined
    );
}
这样 gemini-4-argon 以及未来的 Gemini 4+ 系列模型都会正确分派到 thinkingLevel，问题即可彻底解决。如果需要立即对补丁文件进行修改并应用，请随时告诉我。

Environment

@deepseek-ai/dsh 0.2.0-rc.2 (web), client-plugin runner + @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation 0.2.0-rc.2
Node v22.22.0, Linux (Ubuntu 24.04)

Summary
When two or more plugins register additive list entries on the conversation.view slot, the conversation tab bar renders the same entry twice (identical options.id, duplicate React key) and the intended tab order is not honored.
Related: bowenliang123/dsh-context#137 — the analysis there points at the core (the client-plugin runner forces a negative shadowing priority on additive list slots; slot de-duplication only applies within the same priority; ui-conversation's viewTabs() renders the raw ledger). The plugin side shipped a fix (v0.69.1) and the thread says the core-side issue would be reported here — we could not find that report, so filing it.
Steps to reproduce

Two minimal client plugins, each registering one tab on the conversation.view list slot (distinct options.id, options.order 10 and 20).
Open the web UI with both plugins enabled.

Expected: two tabs, one per registration, in order sequence.
Actual: the slot ledger contains duplicate entries for the same id (once per effective priority), so viewTabs() renders a tab twice; resolveActiveView(viewTabs(), preferred) can settle on either copy non-deterministically; React reports duplicate keys.
Root cause (code reading)

the client-plugin runner forces a negative shadowing priority onto additive list slot registrations;
the slot ledger's de-dupe only drops entries at the same priority — the same id survives once per priority;
viewTabs() in @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation/lib/client.js iterates slots.entries("conversation.view") and renders the raw ledger: no id de-dupe, no order sort.

Workaround in use locally (render-side only, defensive)
const seenViewIds = new Set();
const viewEntries = [...slots.entries("conversation.view")]
  .sort((left, right) => (left.options.order ?? 0) - (right.options.order ?? 0));
for (const entry of viewEntries) {
  if (seenViewIds.has(entry.options.id)) continue;
  seenViewIds.add(entry.options.id);
  // ... mount the tab ...
}
This removes the duplicated tab, but the ledger still contains the duplicate entries (e.g. activateView(sessionId, readConversationViewPreference(sessionId)) paths), so the durable fix belongs in the runner / slot de-dupe: an additive list registration whose id is already present should be merged/replaced, not shadowed at another priority.
Expected behavior: each registered id appears exactly once, entries ordered by options.order.

