dsh-hmr: moduleGraph() throws on CJS children entries without a string filename, disabling plugin-code hot reload
Symptom
On DSH Desktop (packaged build, harness 0.2.1-rc.2), every profile reconciliation that follows a config change logs:
warn hmr: planning module replacement failed; module replacement was not completed
warn hmr: TypeError [ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE]: The "path" argument must be of type string. Received undefined
    at pathToFileURL (node:url:1024:3)
    at Hmr.moduleGraph (…/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:1200:69)
    at async Hmr.planReplacement (…/dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:1215:22)
    at async …/dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:1346:19
    at async Hmr.contained (…/dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:1300:12)
    at async Hmr.reconcileProfile (…/dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:1345:78)
warn hmr: changed modules keep running their previous code until a restart: [{"url":"file:///…/profiles/web/node_modules/<my-plugin>/lib/index.js","reason":"module-comparison"}]```

Consequences:

- **Config-only changes still hot-apply** (the reconciler commits what it can before module planning), so the model list, new plugin entries, etc. take effect live.
- **Changed source of an already-loaded plugin never hot-replaces** — it always falls back to "restart required". Observed 10/10 reconciles failing over ~2.5 h; zero `moduleGraph()` successes in the log.

## Root cause (traced in the shipped code + reproduced in-process)

`@deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr@0.2.1-rc.2` `lib/index.js:1196–1201`:

```js
for (const [filename, module] of Object.entries(commonJsCache())) {
  const children = module === void 0 ? void 0 : Reflect.get(module, "children");
  if (!Array.isArray(children)) continue;
  for (const child of children) add(pathToFileURL(filename).href, pathToFileURL(child.filename).href);
}

Line 1200 dereferences child.filename unguarded. Node normally populates children with real Module instances, but bundled CJS can push synthetic child objects. In my install, a read-only scan of the live host's require.cache (1720 modules, 5098 child edges) found exactly 3 malformed edges, all from the packaged image library:
app.asar/node_modules/sharp/dist/sharp.cjs    child[2] = { exports, loaded }   // no filename
app.asar/node_modules/sharp/dist/libvips.cjs  child[2] = { exports, loaded }
app.asar/node_modules/sharp/dist/utility.cjs  child[4] = { exports, loaded }

So this is not machine-specific: any Electron host that bundles sharp's dist CJS plus any profile plugin will fail every module replacement plan.
Minimal reproduction of the throwing expression:
import { pathToFileURL } from "node:url";
pathToFileURL(({ exports, loaded } /* as child */).filename);
// TypeError [ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE]: The "path" argument must be of type string. Received undefined
Suggested fix
Guard the edge (two lines), same spirit as the typeof found === "string" guards already used elsewhere in the file:
for (const child of children) {
  if (typeof child?.filename !== "string" || child.filename.length === 0) continue;
  add(pathToFileURL(filename).href, pathToFileURL(child.filename).href);
}
Synthetic children carry no cache identity, so skipping their edge cannot lose a real importer: the real requirer is keyed by its own cache path, which the loop already has.
Environment

DSH Desktop packaged (Electron 44, Node 24), harness packages 0.2.1-rc.2, @deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr same
Windows 11, x64
Profile plugin installed via pnpm file: dependency (hardlink copy), also reproduces after converting to a directory junction — the crash happens while building the graph, before any question of which plugin changed

Happy to re-run the in-process cache scan against a fix candidate if that helps.

