DSH-issue-载入历史永久卡住.md
在折腾插件的时候卡死了，花了3个小时修好，deepseek自己建议发一份issue，算是代发

Environment

DeepSeek Harness desktop: 0.2.1-rc.5
macOS

Summary
A plugin whose Config implements Standard Schema validation and exposes toJSON(), but is not a Schemastery schema, can make settings/describe fail. In the desktop app this becomes a fatal desktop welcome: Web RPC failed, preventing startup.
Minimal shape
export const Config = {
  '~standard': {
    version: 1,
    vendor: 'example-plugin',
    validate: (value) => ({ value }),
  },
  toJSON() {
    return { type: 'object', properties: {} };
  },
};
Actual result
After the plugin is loaded, settings/describe returns:
{
  "ok": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "gateway/internal",
    "message": "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'volatile')"
  }
}
The desktop welcome then fails with Web RPC failed.
Cause
Settings.schema(entry) accepts any Config with toJSON(). Settings.describe() passes it to volatileForm(schema), which assumes Schemastery internals (schema.meta.volatile, schema.type, schema.dict). For a valid Standard Schema config, schema.meta may be absent, so enumeration throws before the settings RPC can respond.
Expected
A config schema that the host accepts for plugin configuration should not make settings enumeration crash. Please either validate that the object is a supported Schemastery schema before calling volatileForm, skip unsupported schemas safely, or adapt the supported Standard Schema/JSON Schema representation.
I reproduced this with a linked local plugin using a hand-written Standard Schema config (no Schemastery dependency). Adding Schemastery-shaped markers locally avoids the crash, but the host-side settings service should handle unsupported/non-Schemastery schemas defensively.
